{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "VisualDx API",
    "description": "The VisualDx API is a subscription-based service exposing programmatic access to VisualDx processes, text, and images.\n\n#### All endpoints in the VisualDx API require authentication\n\nOnce you have received your **API Key** and **API Secret**, you may begin accessing the API by following the guide in *Getting Started*.\n\n# Getting Started\n\nThis quick tutorial will provide you and overview of the VisualDx API and outline the steps to get started.\n\n## Setup\n\nThe VisualDx API is a standard RESTful web service that accepts `GET` and `POST` requests.  The current version of the API is available using the base path `https://api.visualdx.com/v1/`. We recommend you build your integrations using a base-path that includes the API version path component.\n\n## Authentication\n\nThe VisualDx API uses a standard Bearer HTTP Authorization header to authenticate your requests. You can use the `/auth/token` endpoint to exchange your credentials for a token.\n\n> If you would like to request API credentials, please [contact us for a \"Sales/Demo Inquiry\"](https://www.visualdx.com/contact/) to set up an API account during our early-access phases.\n\nThe `access_token` provided by the token endpoint is valid for 24 hours, and you may authenticate as many active sessions as you like.\n\n<SecurityDefinitions />\n\n## Text Content\n\nThe VisualDx API returns formatted text content in one of the following formats:\n\n### HTML\n\nText is returned as an HTML fragment using a safe subset of HTML tags:\n\n- `i`\n- `b`\n- `br`\n- `a`\n- `sup`\n- `sub`\n- `ul`\n- `ol`\n- `li`\n\n## VisualDx URI\n\nThe VisualDx API uses a custom URI format to link and locate additional API resources.  References take the following form:\n\n### Diagnoses\n\n      vdx://dx/<id>\n- **id** (number) - the ID of the diagnosis\n\n\n### External Codes\n\n      vdx://code/<system>/<value>\n- **system** (string) - the system for the code\n- **code** (string) - the code value for the given system\n\n## Audience\n\nMost endpoints in the VisualDx API support multiple datasets:\n\n* The **Clinical** dataset exposes all supported _Findings_ and _Conditions_, and content which has been tailored to clinical professionals.\n* The **Consumer** dataset exposes a subset of all supported _Findings_ and _Conditions_, along with content that has been organized and tailored for non-clinical professionals.\n\nEndpoints have been documented with separate requests for each of the Consumer and Clinical \"_audiences_\" in this API documentation. If your account grants access to both audiences, you may make requests to either endpoint freely.\n\n#### Portability of data between Clinical and Consumer audiences\n\nBecause the Consumer audience uses a subset of the _Findings_ and _Conditions_ supported by the Clinical dataset, you may feasibly perform most operations across the boundary presented by the datasets. However there may be unintended consequences of doing this:\n\n* Inference results computed using a Consumer dataset will not attempt to identify some lesions and conditions, which may cause the Clinical Differential endpoint to miss some potential _Conditions_.\n* Submitting _Findings_ or _Conditions_ supported by the Clinical dataset to the Consumer Differential endpoint will result in a loss of these inputs.\n* Attempting to retrieve information about Clinical _Findings_ or _Conditions_ from the Consumer Library Service endpoints will return _HTTP 404: Not Found_.\n",
    "version": "1.0",
    "contact": {
      "name": "API Support",
      "email": "api-support@visualdx.com",
      "url": "https://developers.visualdx.com/"
    },
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://api.swaggerhub.com/apis/healthechartsinc/visualdx-api/1.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://api.visualdx.com/v1/"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Token",
      "description": "Exchange credentials for a token."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inference",
      "description": "Use the **Inference Service** to analyze images and retrieve a weighted set of findings and diagnoses.\n\nResults from the **Inference Service** may be combined with any manually collected findings and submitted to a **Differential Service** endpoint for further analysis.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Differential",
      "description": "Use the **Differential Service** endpoints to create a weighted set of potential condition matches by submitting a weighted set of input findings, diagnoses, and demographic data."
    },
    {
      "name": "Library",
      "description": "Use the **Library Service** to retrieve information about the ID values used in the API, retrieve medical text, and access medical images.\n\nApplications may choose to store responses to some informational endpoints (e.g. *Consumer Findings* and *Consumer Diagnoses*) in a short-lived cache, however updates to the VisualDx API and Data may add, update, or delete Findings and Condition entries.\n"
    },
    {
      "name": "Reference",
      "description": "Static data for use in interpreting API responses.\n\n## Image Types\nImage Type is an integer value returned as part of Image metadata.\nUse the list of Image Types below to display human-readable names for Image Type Ids.\n\n| ImageTypeId | Name                                              | Description                                                           |\n|-------------|---------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 0           | Clinical Image                                    | Clinical image of body region using visible light                     |\n| 17          | Dermoscopic Image                                 | Dermoscopic Image                                                     |\n| 19          | Electrocardiogram                                 | Electrocardiogram                                                     |\n| 4           | Imaging Studies                                   | Non-specific imaging Study                                            |\n| 20          | Imaging Studies > Angiography                     | Angiography                                                           |\n| 11          | Imaging Studies > CT Scan                         | CT Scan                                                               |\n| 16          | Imaging Studies > Echocardiogram                  | Echocardiogram                                                        |\n| 21          | Imaging Studies > Fluoroscopy                     | Fluoroscopy                                                           |\n| 12          | Imaging Studies > MRI Scan                        | MRI Scan                                                              |\n| 15          | Imaging Studies > Nuclear Medicine Scan           | Nuclear Medicine Scan                                                 |\n| 18          | Imaging Studies > PET/CT Scan                     | PET/CT Scan                                                           |\n| 14          | Imaging Studies > Ultrasound                      | Ultrasound                                                            |\n| 13          | Imaging Studies > X-ray                           | X-ray                                                                 |\n| 7           | Irritant or Object Image                          | Image of an irritant or object                                        |\n| 3           | Lab Image                                         | Image of lab results / findings                                       |\n| 23          | Medical graphic                                   | Images of medical algorithms, charts, and other outside illustrations |\n| 10          | Medical Illustration                              | Medical illustration or graphic created by VisualDx                   |\n| 24          | Ophthalmic Imaging                                | Non-specific ophthalmic imaging                                       |\n| 25          | Ophthalmic Imaging > Fundus                       | Fundus (rear eye) image                                               |\n| 8           | Ophthalmic Imaging > Optical Coherence Tomography | Optical Coherence Tomography image                                    |\n| 26          | Ophthalmic Imaging > Slit Lamp Image              | Slit lamp (anterior segment) image                                    |\n| 2           | Organism Image                                    | Image of a non-human organism                                         |\n| 9           | Procedure Image                                   | Image of a clinical procedure or process                              |\n| 22          | Substance                                         | Image of a medication, antidote, illicit drug, or poison              |\n\n## Diagnosis Commonalities\nDiagnosis Commonality is an integer value returned as part of Diagnosis metadata.\nCommonality values range from 1 to 5, with 1 indicating the highest incidence and 5 representing the lowest.\nIncidence rates are based on North American cases.\nUse the list of Commonalities below to display human-readable names for Commonality Ids.\n\n| Commonality | Name                                                    |\n|-------------|---------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1           | Incidence up to 1:100 (Very common)                     |\n| 2           | Incidence between 1:100 and 1:1,000 (Common)            |\n| 3           | Incidence between 1:1,000 and 1:50,000 (Uncommon)       |\n| 4           | Incidence between 1:50,000 and 1:500,000 (Rare)         |\n| 5           | Incidence less frequent than 1:500,000 (Extremely rare) |\n"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "BearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/auth/token": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Obtain a token",
        "tags": [
          "Token"
        ],
        "security": [
          {
            "BasicAuth": []
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "access_token": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "The access token issued by the authorization server."
                    },
                    "expires_in": {
                      "type": "integer",
                      "description": "The lifetime in seconds of the access token."
                    },
                    "token_type": {
                      "type": "string",
                      "description": "The type of the token issued.",
                      "enum": [
                        "Bearer"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "access_token",
                    "expires_in",
                    "token_type"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/inferences/{audience}/image": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Analyze image",
        "tags": [
          "Inference"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "threshold",
            "description": "The minimum confidence threshold to return in the results.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "number",
              "minimum": 0.0,
              "maximum": 1.0,
              "default": 0.001
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "description": "The image to analyze.  A single-layer JPEG or PNG image, up to a maximum file-size of 10mb, and a maximum pixel-count of approximately 3MP (3,145,728 pixels). Ensure that the feature you want analyzed occupies the center 75% of the image.",
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "image/png": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "binary"
              }
            },
            "image/jpeg": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "string",
                "format": "binary"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "data": {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Inference"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "data"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "415": {
            "description": "The image format is not supported."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/differentials/{audience}/workup": {
      "post": {
        "summary": "Get a differential",
        "description": "This request returns a list of diagnosis matches given a differential request.  At least one finding or diagnosis must be sent.",
        "tags": [
          "Differential"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/textFormat"
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Workup"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Differential"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/BadRequest"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/images/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get an image",
        "description": "Retrieve an image from the library in the specified size.\n\nPossible image types:\n- `image/jpeg`\n- `image/png`\n\n> Note: This request may return a redirect (`HTTP 302` with `Location` header).\n",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "id",
            "description": "The unique identifier for the image.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "integer"
            }
          },
          {
            "in": "query",
            "name": "size",
            "description": "The desired size of the image.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "thumbnail",
                "standard",
                "large",
                "full"
              ],
              "default": "standard"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "302": {
            "description": "Image found.  Clients should follow the `Location` header to download.",
            "headers": {
              "Location": {
                "description": "The URI where the client can download the image.",
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "uri"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/findings/categories": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get finding categories",
        "description": "This request returns a list of finding categories applicable to the given audience.",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "data": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "type": "string"
                      },
                      "example": [
                        "Appearance",
                        "Lesion",
                        "Distribution"
                      ]
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "data"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/findings/categories/{category}": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get findings",
        "description": "This request returns a list of findings belonging to the given category applicable to the given audience.",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "in": "path",
            "name": "category",
            "description": "The category for which to retrieve findings.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "data": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FindingSummary"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "data"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/findings/{id}": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get finding",
        "description": "This request returns the finding that corresponds to the given audience and id.",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/conceptId"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "data": {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FindingSummary"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "data"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/findings/search": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Search findings by name",
        "description": "Performs a search for Findings which match the specified query. Searches across Finding names, alternative names, and definitions. Does not search external codes, medical text, or citations.",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/searchQuery"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "data": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "maxItems": 20,
                      "items": {
                        "allOf": [
                          {
                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FindingSummary"
                          },
                          {
                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TextSearch"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "data"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/findings/search/by-code": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Search findings by code",
        "description": "Performs a search for Findings which match the specified code and system.",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/externalCodeValue"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/externalCodeSystem"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "data": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FindingSummary"
                      }
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "data"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/diagnoses": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Get diagnoses",
        "description": "This request returns a list of diagnoses applicable to the specified audience.",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageNumber"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/pageCapacity"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/textFormat"
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "properties": {
                    "data": {
                      "type": "array",
                      "items": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/DiagnosisSummary"
                      }
                    },
                    "page": {
                      "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PageInfo"
                    }
                  },
                  "required": [
                    "data",
                    "page"
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthorized"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Forbidden"
          },
          "404": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/NotFound"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/libraries/{audience}/diagnoses/search": {
      "get": {
        "summary": "Search diagnoses by name",
        "description": "Search for Diagnoses that match the specified query. Searches across Diagnosis names, alternative names, and definitions. Does not search external codes, medical text, or citations.",
        "tags": [
          "Library"
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/audience"
          },
          {
            "$ref": "#/components/parameters/searchQuery"
